Abstract We show that Sarnak’s conjecture on Möbius disjointness holds in every uniquely ergodic model of a quasi-discrete spectrum automorphism. A consequence of this result is that, for each non constant polynomial <tex xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">$P\in{{\BBR}}[x]$</tex> with irrational leading coefficient and for each multiplicative function <tex xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">${\mbi {
u}}:{{\BBN}}	o{{\BBC}}$</tex>, <tex xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">$|{\mbi {
u}}|\leq1$</tex>, we have <tex xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">$$\matrix{ {{1 \over M}\mathop \sum \limits_{M \le m \lt 2M} {1 \over H}\left| {\mathop \sum \limits_{m \le n \lt m + H} {e^{2\pi iP(n)}}
u (n)} ight|0} \cr } $$</tex> as <tex xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">$M	o\infty$</tex>, <tex xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">$H	o\infty$</tex>, <tex xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">$H/M	o 0$</tex>.
